<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Danton's Death</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1835</span> · Also known as Dantons Tod</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Danton's Death is a play by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georg-buchner">Georg Büchner</a>, written in 1835 while he was hiding from the Hessian police after publishing a revolutionary pamphlet. It portrays the last days of the French revolutionary Georges Danton before his execution under Robespierre's Terror, using speeches from historical sources. It was first staged in 1902 and is now a classic of German drama.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dantons-death.jpg" alt="Danton's Death" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Katja Rehfeld · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-Z0420-027,_Berlin,_%22Dantons_Tod%22.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
